A cornerstone of Lone Star State comfort food. Rather than relying on canned condensed cream soups, this updated King Ranch casserole harnesses the tangy brightness of jarred tomatillo salsa verde, roasted green chiles, and cool sour cream. Layered like a Mexican lasagna between torn corn tortillas and plenty of melted cheese.

*Adapted from [A Spicy Perspective](https://www.aspicyperspective.com/king-ranch-chicken-casserole/#recipe).*

## Ingredients

- 5 cups cooked chicken (leftover roasted chicken or shredded meat from 1 large rotisserie chicken)
- 2 cups full-fat sour cream
- 1 large yellow onion, finely diced
- 4 cloves garlic, minced
- 1 tablespoon unsalted butter
- 1 jar (16 oz) tomatillo salsa verde (mild or medium)
- 1 can (13.5 oz) diced green chiles (or two 7-oz cans, undrained)
- ½ cup fresh cilantro, chopped
- 2 teaspoons ground cumin
- 4 cups shredded Mexican-blend cheese (cheddar, Monterey Jack, Asadero), divided
- 20 small white corn tortillas, torn by hand into rough 2-inch pieces

## Instructions

1. **Preheat and Prep:** Preheat your oven to 400°F (200°C). Lightly grease a deep 9x13-inch (3-quart) ceramic or glass casserole dish with cooking spray or butter.
2. **Sauté the Aromatics:** Set a skillet over medium heat and melt 1 tablespoon of butter. Add the diced yellow onion and minced garlic. Sauté for 3 to 5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the onions are tender, aromatic, and translucent. Pull the pan from the heat.
3. **Mix the Creamy Chicken Filling:** In a large mixing bowl, combine the shredded chicken, sour cream, salsa verde, undrained diced green chiles, chopped cilantro, ground cumin, and the sautéed onion and garlic mixture. Stir with a large spatula until completely homogenized into a rich, creamy Tex-Mex sauce.
4. **Tear the Tortillas:** Tear the white corn tortillas into rough 2-inch irregular pieces. (Tearing instead of leaving whole allows the casserole to slice easily without sliding apart).
5. **Layer the Casserole:**
   - **Base Layer:** Spread one-quarter of the chicken mixture across the bottom of the prepared baking dish.
   - **First Cheese & Tortilla:** Sprinkle 1 cup of the shredded cheese, then scatter one-third of the torn tortilla pieces in an even single layer.
   - **Repeat:** Repeat this sequence two more times (chicken, cheese, tortillas), using up all the remaining torn tortillas.
   - **Crown:** Spread the final one-quarter of the chicken mixture across the top tortilla layer and cover evenly with the final 1 cup of shredded cheese.
6. **Bake to Golden Bubbles:** Transfer to the oven and bake uncovered at 400°F for 20 to 25 minutes. The casserole is done when the edges are bubbling energetically and the top cheese is golden brown and melted.
7. **Rest and Serve:** Remove from the oven and allow the casserole to settle on the counter for 5 to 10 minutes before cutting. This brief rest lets the corn tortillas absorb the sauce and firm up into neat, sliceable portions. Garnish with extra cilantro and serve warm.

## Notes

- **Rotisserie Chicken Shortcut:** One standard supermarket rotisserie chicken yields roughly 4 to 5 cups of shredded meat, making prep under 15 minutes.
- **Make-Ahead:** Assemble the casserole completely, cover tightly with plastic wrap and foil, and refrigerate for up to 24 hours. When ready to bake, remove plastic wrap, cover with foil, and bake at 375°F for 30 minutes, then uncover for 10 minutes to brown the cheese.
